Changes: tables were selected, joined and cleaned; training spots were derived from monster
levels and spawns; each monster keeps its five likeliest drops; quest texts were shortened.

The pictures of monsters, items, NPCs and skills in a pack of format 3 or later are NEXON's game
art, as the MapleClassic Wiki shows them, included for identification only. They are covered
neither by the wiki's license nor by Dravix's; NEXON holds their copyright.

The packs hold no code. MapleStory is a trademark of NEXON Korea Corporation. Dravix is not
